#: ../../../pro/reports/reports.md:3
msgid "You can work on the `sheet`, `book` or `app` level:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../pro/reports/reports.md:5
msgid ""
"`mysheet.render_template(**data)`: replaces the placeholders in `mysheet`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../pro/reports/reports.md:6
msgid ""
"`mybook.render_template(**data)`: replaces the placeholders in all sheets of "
"`mybook`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../pro/reports/reports.md:7
msgid ""
"`myapp.render_template(template, output, **data)`: convenience wrapper that "
"copies a template book before replacing the placeholder with the values. "
"Since this approach allows you to work with hidden Excel instances, it is "
"the most commonly used method for production."
msgstr ""

